; QUUX's band carries no Chaos after step R3 (QUUX's Ethernet contract,
; section 8): a census of the files loaded and of the CHAOS: symbols in
; compiled code finds 0 (lisp/chaos-census.lisp).  On a band built before R3
; the NCP and its services are loaded, and the census finds them: its
; failing cases are the check's control, and the recorded ones say what was
; found.
;
; The census looks: the band has loaded files, and has FEFs, walked from
; every structure region with no failed walk
(plusp (census-loaded-files)) => T
(let ((f (census-fefs))) (list (> (car f) 1000) (cadr f))) => (T 0)
; Chaos's files loaded: none
(census-files) => NIL
; (FEF, CHAOS: symbol) pairs in compiled code: none
(census-symbols) => 0
; CHAOS: symbols in the interpreted forms of the initialization lists: none
(census-initializations) => NIL
; recorded: the FEFs walked, all files loaded, and the files whose FEFs name
; a CHAOS: symbol, with their pairs
(census-fefs)
(census-loaded-files)
(census-hits-by-file)
; recorded: the pairs whose FEF's defining file is not known
(census-hits-unattributed)
